[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
jawas reads /usr/local/etc/jawas/config.toml (template installed as
config.toml.sample). Install the dump tools of the engines you back up:

  mysql84-client or mariadb114-client   (mysqldump / mariadb-dump)
  postgresql18-client                   (pg_dump, pg_dumpall, psql)
  sqlite3                               (sqlite3)
  age                                   (only with [encryption])
  rclone                                (only with a [[remote]] of type rclone)

On a host that receives backups over ssh ([[remote]] of type ssh), no
configuration is needed: give the sender's key a forced command in
~/.ssh/authorized_keys:

  command="jawas receive -S /srv/jawas/web1 --apply",restrict ssh-ed25519 AAAA...

and rotate there with: jawas prune -S /srv/jawas/web1 --apply

then check and schedule it:

  jawas check
  jawas backup                  # dry-run
  printf '%s\n' 'PATH=/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin' \
    '15 3 * * * root jawas backup --apply --quiet' > /usr/local/etc/cron.d/jawas

(cron's default PATH lacks /usr/local/bin, where the dump tools live).
EOM
}
]
